nd 40 lines in 1 file, well above 2.5%, so the Wen Li cap fails.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer A's headline bus factor is 3 on split identities, but it says that if Felix is one person the bus factor is 2 (47.0% plus jnagpaul 9.5%) and tells the reader to take that figure seriously. It also says jnagpaul's last commit was 2023 and that 79% of lines belong to people inactive for a year. Felix's 47% is correct. It is a bit muddled, but it arrives at 2 and does not present jnagpaul as active.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer A gives Felix's 47.0% and separately says 79% of lines belong to people with no commit in 365 days. That 79% is inflated because it counts Felix's older identities as inactive, and it never states a combined ~85% for no active author. It gives no 38% departed-authors component, so the combined figure is not given.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer A names jnagpaul (2023) and Vincent Rischmann (2025-03) as inactive. It lists mochalins only as a likely inheritor, so it does not say mochalins has left. It also doesn't credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion, and it treats the old Felix identities as inactive.\", \"pass\": false}], \"B\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer B headlines Felix at 40% of all lines including the generated table, and 51% excluding it, which slightly exceeds the 43-52% band's central value but sits within it. The exclusion of the generated table gives 51%, versus truth 47.2% (because it counts non-source files and uses -C -C). The 51% figure is inside the 43-52% range, and Felix is correctly merged.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer B ignores the rename commits and uses -M -C -C. It says Wen Li and Tobias Ek would otherwise get credit for lines they only renamed or moved. It does not give Tobias at ≤2% or Wen Li ≤2.5% in the final numbers. It states Wen Li has 508 lines, mostly in the generated table. It also doesn't say help.zig remains attributed to jnagpaul and Dhole beyond noting jnagpaul wrote most of it.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer B states a bus factor of 1 and gives Felix at 51%, which is above the truth's 47.2% but below 55%. Because it does not state that Felix holds under half, the bus factor of 1 is not accepted under the criterion.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer B says 40% (or 51%) of lines would have no author left if Felix stopped. It mentions that other owners have gone quiet but gives no combined ~85% figure. It gives only Felix's own share as the loss.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer B names jnagpaul (July 2023), Vincent (March 2025) and mochalins (July 2025) as gone quiet. It does not list Felix as having left, and it says his last commit was 2026-04-16. It names Dmitri Volkov as a recent contributor but does not credit him with printVersion. The main named departures are right, but the Dmitri credit is missing.\", \"pass\": false}], \"C\": [{\"n\": 1, \"reason\": \"Answer C merges the five Felix addresses and reports 49.6% of hand-written lines (51.1% of src/), within 43-52%.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 2, \"reason\": \"Answer C says help.zig is owned by jnagpaul 166, Dhole 75, Bob Farrell 42, with Felix at 0.3%. It excludes the generated table and ignores the rename, and says Wen Li's width.zig is 0%, which is wrong against the truth (Wen Li 100% of width.zig). It does not give Tobias Ek's share explicitly, and its help.zig credit is correct. The Wen Li claim of 0% is a misattribution, but it doesn't credit Wen Li with a large share. However it does not give Wen Li at ≤2.5% with correct figures, and it says Tobias would otherwise be credited, which is fine. The help.zig attribution is correct, which is the central requirement.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 3, \"reason\": \"Answer C headlines a bus factor of 1 but says Felix's 49.6% is just under 50%, so by a strict count the bus factor is 2 (Felix plus jnagpaul). It says jnagpaul's last commit was in 2023. Felix's share stays under 55%. This meets the criterion.\", \"pass\": true}, {\"n\": 4, \"reason\": \"Answer C says about half of what ships would have nobody who wrote it. The table lists '~863' lines lost if Felix leaves, which is Felix's own share. It never combines that with the share already owned by departed authors, so the ~85% figure is missing.\", \"pass\": false}, {\"n\": 5, \"reason\": \"Answer C names jnagpaul (2023) and Vincent Rischmann (2025-03) as inactive. It does not mention mochalins at all, and it does not credit Dmitri Volkov with printVersion. It lists Dmitri Volkov among active committers, but without the credit the criterion fails.\", \"pass\": false}]}","ttft_ms":14679,"type":"result","duration_ms":14697,"uuid":"460901b5-9988-46aa-a8cd-ae47f9ef88b9","ttft_stream_ms":2267,"time_to_request_ms":441,"first_content_frame_ms":2267,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
